# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE RECOVERY CHECKLIST — names only, no values.
#
# Regenerated 2026-08-11 by grepping every `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_*`
# (Next.js build), `env.X` (Cloudflare Functions), `Deno.env.get("X")`
# (Supabase Edge Functions), and `supabase.rpc(...)` (Supabase Vault
# indirection) reference in this codebase — generated from what the code
# actually reads at runtime, not guessed, not carried over from the prior
# version of this file. The prior version (last regenerated 2026-08-01)
# was missing TAVILY_API_KEY entirely and did not document the Vault path
# at all — both are real, load-bearing dependencies added since. If a
# fresh grep of src/, functions/, and supabase/functions/ ever finds a
# name not listed here, THIS file is stale — regenerate it, don't
# hand-edit it out of sync.
#
# Nothing below is a secret. Actual values live in FOUR separate places —
# not three. Losing track of this is the single most common way this
# system quietly breaks after a rebuild or a credential rotation:
#   1. This repo's local .env.local (gitignored, exists only on your
#      machine — not backed up by git).
#   2. Cloudflare Pages dashboard (Settings → Environment Variables, and
#      separately, Settings → Functions → Secrets — these are TWO
#      different sections inside Cloudflare, not one).
#   3. Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → Edge Functions → Secrets.
#   4. Supabase dashboard → Vault (a DIFFERENT store from #3, read only
#      via an RPC call, not via Deno.env.get — see section 4 below).
# A name appearing in more than one store below means the SAME value
# must be kept in sync by hand across those stores independently —
# nothing here propagates automatically.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 1. Cloudflare build-time (.env.local locally; also Cloudflare Pages
#      → Settings → Environment Variables for the production build) ──
# Read directly by Next.js at build time via process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
# Anything NEXT_PUBLIC_ ships into the browser bundle — never put a real
# secret behind this prefix.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# Client-side admin-panel UI gating ONLY — this is NOT a real security
# boundary (it's visible in the shipped bundle; real enforcement is the
# server-side ADMIN_EMAILS in section 2). Read as a fallback chain:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOWED_ADMIN_EMAIL, then NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_EMAILS, then a
# HARDCODED two-address default baked into src/app/admin/layout.tsx and
# src/components/PostHogProvider.tsx if neither is set. Set
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOWED_ADMIN_EMAIL explicitly in production so the
# hardcoded fallback is never the one actually in effect.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOWED_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# Legacy fallback for the above — both are still read; consolidate to
# just NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOWED_ADMIN_EMAIL when convenient, not urgent.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_EMAILS=

# Optional — client-side analytics. System functions fully without it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=


# ── 2. Cloudflare Pages → Settings → Functions → Secrets ──
# Read by functions/api/*.ts via the `env` argument passed into each
# handler. Reconfigure these in the Cloudflare dashboard for this Pages
# project if rebuilding. (env.ASSETS also appears in this runtime but is
# a Cloudflare Pages platform binding, not a user-configured secret —
# nothing to set for it.)

ADMIN_EMAILS=
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
PAGESPEED_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
RESEND_API_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
# Optional — server-side analytics event capture. System degrades
# gracefully without it.
POSTHOG_API_KEY=


# ── 3. Supabase → Project Settings → Edge Functions → Secrets ──
# Read by supabase/functions/*/index.ts via Deno.env.get(). Reconfigure
# these under the Supabase project's Edge Function secrets if rebuilding —
# separate from Cloudflare's copies above, even where the name matches
# (SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, STRIPE_SECRET_KEY,
# POSTHOG_API_KEY all exist independently in both section 2 and section 3).

SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Load-bearing for prospecting-suggest-leads AND prospecting-discover-contact
# (contact enrichment) — both features fail with configuration_missing /
# a 502 without this. Confirmed present in code via direct grep; was
# MISSING from this file's prior version.
TAVILY_API_KEY=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_PRICE_CERTIFIED_ANNUAL=
STRIPE_PRICE_CERTIFIED_MONTHLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_CERTIFIED_RENEWAL=
# Optional — same graceful-degradation note as section 2.
POSTHOG_API_KEY=
# Optional — outreach-scanner only sends its Slack alert when this is set
# (`if (slackWebhookUrl)`); absent means silently skipped, not broken.
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=


# ── 4. Supabase → Vault (NOT the same store as section 3 — read via an
#      RPC call, not Deno.env.get) ──
# functions/api/diagnose.ts (a Cloudflare Function, not a Deno Edge
# Function) retrieves ANTHROPIC_API_KEY through
# `supabase.rpc('get_anthropic_key')` rather than reading it from
# Cloudflare's own secret store. This means ANTHROPIC_API_KEY effectively
# needs to exist in BOTH section 3 (for Deno Edge Functions using
# ai-router.ts's "blade" tier) AND here (for the admin AI Diagnostic
# Engine specifically) — two independent copies of the same value, in two
# different systems, with no automatic sync between them.
#
# Set up via: Supabase dashboard → Vault → create a secret, then run
#   select vault.create_secret('<the real key>', 'anthropic_api_key');
# and confirm the `get_anthropic_key()` RPC function exists and returns
# it. If functions/api/diagnose.ts starts returning "Vault retrieval
# failed — ANTHROPIC_API_KEY not initialized", this is the store to check
# — section 3 being correctly set will NOT fix that error.


# ── Recovery order, if rebuilding on a new machine ──
# 1. Clone the repo from GitHub (this file travels with it).
# 2. Recreate .env.local from section 1 above — values come from the
#    Supabase dashboard (Project Settings → API) and/or Cloudflare Pages'
#    existing environment variables if that project is still live.
# 3. Confirm section 2's values are still set in Cloudflare Pages (they
#    persist independently of this laptop — nothing to do unless the
#    Cloudflare project itself was also lost).
# 4. Confirm section 3's values are still set in Supabase Edge Function
#    secrets (same — independent of this laptop).
# 5. Confirm section 4's Vault secret independently — it is NOT the same
#    store as section 3 even though the key name matches.
# 6. npm install && npm run build to verify the local build still works
#    end to end before deploying anything.
